FACTIONS:- 

CORNERSTONE:- 
The Cornerstone Group is a faction of the Conservative Party that represents socially conservative and traditionalist views. Members of this group often advocate for issues such as family values, religious freedom, and a strong national identity. It includes MPs who seek to maintain a more traditional approach to social and moral issues.

CONSERVATIVE WAY FORWARD:-
Conservative Way Forward is a prominent conservative organisation within the party. It has supported policies promoting free-market economics, individual liberty, and a strong national defence. This group often aligns with Thatcherite and libertarian ideals and has been influential in shaping the party's direction

TORY REFORM GROUP:-
The Tory Reform Group is a more centrist faction within the Conservative Party. It has advocated for a more socially liberal and moderate approach, emphasising issues like environmental conservation, social justice, and civil liberties. TRG members tend to align with "One Nation” conservatism.





